---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="AI Models, Gateway & Smart Routing" 
  description="Multi-tier model redundancy, automated fallback cascades, LiteLLM gateway configuration, and model selection syntax."
  category="AI Intelligence"
  prevPage={{ title: "Standalone / Raspberry Pi Install", href: `${baseUrl}/docs/standalone-install` }}
  nextPage={{ title: "Telegram Bot Handbook", href: `${baseUrl}/docs/telegram` }}
>
  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    <strong>🧠 Resilient AI Gateway Architecture:</strong><br />
    The Agent Station routes all AI queries through a local <code>litellm-proxy</code> container on port <code>4000</code>. If an upstream provider suffers rate limiting (HTTP 429) or server outages (HTTP 500/503), the gateway seamlessly cascades to the next healthy model in milliseconds with zero dropped messages.
  </div>

